title: [+ kwasniewski_call_title +]
subtitle: The former president has an opinion about whatever we are currently stuck in, and a telephone.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_party_card
frequency: 110
view-if: month_actions < max_month_actions and kwasniewski_channel = 1 and kwasniewski_estranged = 0 and kwasniewski_alignment >= 50 and kwasniewski_card_timer <= 0
card-image: img/poland/cards/kwasniewski-call.webp
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; kwasniewski_card_timer = 5; kwasniewski_call_count += 1

# The aligned Kwaśniewski deck. One card, seven faces. Both the title and the
# tailored option are selected in poland_normalize before the hand is dealt,
# because the player has to be able to read the title in the hand. The frame is
# the year's own argument; the topic is the worst live problem he could
# plausibly help with. He never gains an office and never gains a vote.

= [+ kwasniewski_call_title +]

[? if kwasniewski_frame = "aftermath": The invitation arrives on foundation
letterhead in the flat, exhausted weeks after a presidential election, when
nobody in Polish politics is quite sure yet what the result meant.?]
[? if kwasniewski_frame = "primacy": The invitation arrives in the month the
Tribunal is being asked whether the treaties bind Poland at all. He negotiated
those treaties. He has been unbearable about it on television for a fortnight,
and he intends to continue.?]
[? if kwasniewski_frame = "war": The invitation arrives with a war on the other
side of the eastern border and half the country's spare rooms full of people
who fled it. He has spent the month on foreign broadcasters explaining Poland
to audiences who have suddenly remembered it exists.?]
[? if kwasniewski_frame = "count": The invitation arrives in the year the
opposition finally has to do arithmetic instead of rhetoric, which is the only
kind of year he has ever really enjoyed.?]
[? if kwasniewski_frame = "repair": The invitation arrives while every
institution in the country is being repaired by people arguing about what
repair means. He has views on all of it, and the constitutional lawyers keep
citing his signature.?]
[? if kwasniewski_frame = "palace": The invitation arrives during a
presidential year, which for him is not a season but a personal anniversary.?]
[? if kwasniewski_frame = "third_winter": The invitation arrives in the
coalition's third winter, the point at which, in his experience, governments
stop being judged on what they promised and start being judged on what they
have become.?]
[? if kwasniewski_frame = "election_year": The invitation arrives in an
election year, and he does not pretend it is about anything else.?]

There is no agenda and no press. There is coffee, a folder he has clearly read,
and **Aleksander Kwaśniewski** sitting in a room we did not book, in a
conversation we did not start, about a problem he has already diagnosed.

[? if kwasniewski_topic = "candidate": He wants to talk about our candidate.
Specifically, he wants to talk about the fact that a great many voters have not
yet decided whether our candidate is a serious person, and that this is a
solvable problem which the campaign is currently not solving. He knows it is
solvable because it was his problem in 1995 and he solved it in eight weeks.?]
[? if kwasniewski_topic = "bloc": He wants to talk about the democratic camp,
which he says is currently conducting three separate wars and one election. He
has already spoken to the others. He would like to say a sentence in public
that makes it marginally more embarrassing for any of them to continue.?]
[? if kwasniewski_topic = "ko": He wants to talk about **[+ ko_leader +]**,
whom he has known for thirty years, likes intermittently, and can telephone
without an appointment. The relationship between our parties is deteriorating
faster than either side's public statements admit, and he thinks it is
recoverable this month and not next.?]
[? if kwasniewski_topic = "partner": He wants to talk about the people who have
stopped taking our calls. He has, over three decades, accumulated a Rolodex
that includes almost every person in Polish public life who has ever held an
office, and a striking number of them owe him something they would rather not
be reminded of.?]
[? if kwasniewski_topic = "old_electorate": He wants to talk about the voters
he keeps meeting at book signings: sixty-five, provincial, voted for him twice,
have not voted for anybody since. He is careful to say that he cannot bring us
a single voter under forty, and slightly too pleased about how carefully he
says it.?]
[? if kwasniewski_topic = "surge": He wants to talk about our polling, which he
has been watching with the specific attention of a man who once held the
numbers we are approaching. He is not offering advice so much as offering to be
seen agreeing with us in public while it lasts.?]
[? if kwasniewski_topic = "unity": He wants to talk about our own party, which
he says is currently the noisiest organisation in Poland and the least
audible. He has, he notes, presided over exactly this and would like to save us
the eight years it took him to learn nothing from it.?]

- @call_candidate
- @call_bloc
- @call_ko
- @call_partner
- @call_old_electorate
- @call_surge
- @call_unity
- @call_trade
- @call_decline


@call_candidate
title: Let him vouch for the candidate, at length and by name
subtitle: A former president saying our nominee is ready is worth more than a month of our own advertising, and costs the campaign its own voice for a week.
view-if: kwasniewski_topic = "candidate"
on-arrival: {!
Q.kwasniewski_standing += 1;
Q.kwasniewski_alignment_bias += 2;
Q.winner_reputation += 6;
Q.list_confidence += 4;
Q.media_access += 4;
Q.leadership_authority += 2;
Q.pensioner_support += 3;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.pres_bonus_left = (Number(Q.pres_bonus_left) || 0) + 0.4;
Q.pres_2025_campaign_strength =
    (Number(Q.pres_2025_campaign_strength) || 0) + 3;
Q.razem_dissent += 3;
Q.progressives_dissent += 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "A former president vouches for the Left's candidate by name and at length";
!}

He does it the way he does everything, which is thoroughly. Not a sentence of
endorsement but forty minutes of it: the programme, the biography, the specific
reasons a person who has never held national office can hold this one. Studios
that had our candidate down as a curiosity re-book them as a contender.

For about a week the campaign is a story about him. That is the exchange rate,
and it is a good one.

- #poland_card_finish


@call_bloc
title: Let him say the sentence about what unites the democratic parties
subtitle: Lowers the temperature across the whole camp for a while. Nobody's grievance is resolved; everybody's grievance becomes harder to broadcast.
view-if: kwasniewski_topic = "bloc"
on-arrival: {!
Q.kwasniewski_standing += 2;
Q.kwasniewski_alignment_bias += 3;
Q.government_coalition_dissent -= 8;
Q.opposition_list_pressure = Math.max(
    0,
    (Number(Q.opposition_list_pressure) || 0) - 1
);
Q.ko_relation += 3;
Q.p2050_relation += 3;
Q.psl_relation += 3;
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.institutional_trust += 1;
Q.razem_dissent += 3;
Q.progressives_dissent += 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "A former president tells the democratic parties in public that there is more that unites them";
!}

The sentence is banal, which is the point. He says it on the main evening
programme, with the leaders of three parties having been told in advance that
he was going to, and for a fortnight every negotiator in the camp who wants to
brief against another one has to decide whether to be the person who made the
old man look naive.

It resolves nothing. It buys the time in which resolving things is possible,
and it is the only instrument in Polish politics that produces that particular
commodity.

- #poland_card_finish


@call_ko
title: Let him telephone [+ ko_leader +] before this becomes permanent
subtitle: Stops the slide with KO while it is still a quarrel rather than a rupture. He will not ask our permission for what he says.
view-if: kwasniewski_topic = "ko"
on-arrival: {!
Q.kwasniewski_standing += 1;
Q.kwasniewski_alignment_bias += 3;
Q.ko_relation += 9;
Q.government_coalition_dissent -= 4;
Q.p2050_relation += 1;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.negotiation_capital += 2;
Q.razem_dissent += 4;
Q.progressives_dissent += 2;
Q.party_unity -= 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "A former president intervenes before the Left and KO stop speaking altogether";
!}

The call happens the same evening, and we are not on it. What comes back is an
agreement that both parties' spokesmen will stop answering questions about each
other for a month, a restored channel between the two general secretaries, and
the distinct impression that he told them the same thing he told us.

Our own left points out, correctly, that the person repairing our relationship
with the largest liberal party has a lifelong preference for us being inside it.

- #poland_card_finish


@call_partner
title: Open the Rolodex and find out who still owes him a favour
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Reopens the parties and figures who had stopped negotiating with us; the debts he calls in are his, not ours.
view-if: kwasniewski_topic = "partner"
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: There is nobody free to staff a fortnight of somebody else's introductions.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.kwasniewski_standing += 2;
Q.kwasniewski_alignment_bias += 2;
Q.psl_relation += 6;
Q.p2050_relation += 6;
Q.ko_relation += 2;
Q.negotiation_capital += 5;
Q.government_coalition_dissent -= 4;
Q.local_network += 2;
Q.institutional_trust += 1;
Q.razem_dissent += 3;
Q.news_headline =
    "Doors that had closed on Lewica reopen through a former president's address book";
!}

It is not glamorous work and he does not pretend otherwise. Eleven telephone
calls over nine days: a former minister here, a marshal of a voivodeship there,
two people whose careers he made in 1997 and one whose career he ended.
Everyone takes the call. Most of them agree to take ours afterwards.

What we have bought is access, not agreement, and it is rented rather than
owned. But the rooms we could not get into last month are rooms we can get into
now.

- #poland_card_finish


@call_old_electorate
title: Send him to the voters who stopped voting after 2005
subtitle: Stabilises the older, provincial, post-SLD electorate. It does approximately nothing for anybody under forty, and he says so himself.
view-if: kwasniewski_topic = "old_electorate"
on-arrival: {!
Q.kwasniewski_standing += 1;
Q.kwasniewski_alignment_bias += 2;
Q.pensioner_support += 5;
Q.workers_support += 2;
Q.rural_support += 1;
Q.young_support -= 1;
Q.left_poll += 0.2;
Q.turnout_readiness += 2;
Q.barons_strength += 1;
Q.barons_dissent -= 3;
Q.progressives_dissent += 3;
Q.razem_dissent += 3;
Q.progressive_credibility -= 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "A former president spends a month with the electorate that stopped voting after 2005";
!}

Cultural centres, library halls, a district pensioners' association in
Piotrków, and one regional radio station where the presenter cries. They come
for him and they stay to hear our housing figures, which is not the same thing
as agreeing with them, but it is the difference between a demographic that is
lost and a demographic that is merely disappointed.

He warned us in the meeting and repeats it in the car afterwards: he cannot
deliver a single voter under forty, and any campaign built on his audience is a
campaign with a mortality table attached.

- #poland_card_finish


@call_surge
title: Let him be seen agreeing with us while the numbers last
subtitle: Converts a good polling month into the appearance of a governing party. He is enjoying this more than we are.
view-if: kwasniewski_topic = "surge"
on-arrival: {!
Q.kwasniewski_standing += 1;
Q.kwasniewski_alignment_bias += 2;
Q.winner_reputation += 5;
Q.electoral_viability += 4;
Q.leadership_authority += 3;
Q.media_capacity += 3;
Q.media_access += 2;
Q.left_poll_momentum = (Number(Q.left_poll_momentum) || 0) + 0.15;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.razem_dissent += 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "A former president spends the month agreeing with the Left in public";
!}

He goes on everything. He treats our programme as a governing programme rather
than a protest, refers to our leader by office rather than by name, and answers
the question about whether the Left can actually run a ministry as though it
were a stupid question, which is the single most useful thing anyone can do for
a party at this stage.

At some point in every interview he mentions his own numbers in 2000. Nobody
has ever been able to stop him doing this and nobody ever will.

- #poland_card_finish


@call_unity
title: Let him lecture our own factions, in one room, with the door shut
subtitle: An outsider nobody in the party can outrank says the thing our leadership cannot say without it being a factional move.
view-if: kwasniewski_topic = "unity"
on-arrival: {!
Q.kwasniewski_standing += 1;
Q.kwasniewski_alignment_bias += 2;
Q.party_unity += 5;
Q.organiser_energy += 2;
Q.public_trust += 1;
for (const faction of Q.factions) {
    Q[faction + "_dissent"] -= 2;
}
Q.razem_dissent += 3;
Q.news_headline =
    "A former president spends an afternoon telling the Left's factions what happened to his";
!}

He does not mediate, because he has nothing to offer any of them. He simply
describes, for ninety minutes and without notes, what happened to the last
Polish left party that could not stop arguing in public: the offices, the
membership, the electorate, the year each of them went, and the name of every
person who was certain at the time that their faction was the one being
persecuted.

Nobody in the room can outrank him and nobody in the room enjoys it. The
temperature drops for a while, which is all an outsider was ever going to
achieve.

- #poland_card_finish


@call_trade
title: Spend the meeting on us instead of on the problem
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Ignore what he came to fix and use the afternoon to bank his authority against a later negotiation.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Banking a favour requires somebody free to keep the relationship warm.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.kwasniewski_standing += 3;
Q.kwasniewski_alignment_bias += 1;
Q.negotiation_capital += 6;
Q.media_access += 2;
Q.ko_relation += 2;
Q.p2050_relation += 1;
Q.public_trust -= 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica banks a former president's goodwill instead of spending it on this month's crisis";
!}

We let him talk, we agree with him, and we do not do the thing he came to
suggest. Instead we spend the afternoon on the relationship itself: the joint
appearance in the autumn, the foundation panel, the introduction he will make
when the negotiation that actually matters arrives.

He notices. He has been on the other side of this manoeuvre for forty years and
recognises it immediately, and he allows it, because a politician who is
planning three moves ahead is a politician he approves of on principle.

- #poland_card_finish


@call_decline
title: Take the coffee and commit to nothing
subtitle: Free. Hear him out, keep the relationship, and let the party solve its own problem this month.
on-arrival: {!
Q.kwasniewski_alignment_bias -= 1;
Q.party_unity += 1;
Q.progressive_credibility += 2;
Q.razem_dissent -= 2;
Q.progressives_dissent -= 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica hears out a former president and announces nothing";
!}

We drink the coffee, we take the folder, and we tell him honestly that this one
is ours to sort out. He is neither offended nor surprised; a man who has been
offering unsolicited advice to Polish party leaders since 1990 has calibrated
expectations.

The line stays open. The problem stays ours.

- #poland_card_finish
